# InodeFence user settings for the `inodefence` command (example).
#
# Copy to ~/.config/inodefence/config.env (or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/inodefence/config.env, or any file
# named by INODEFENCE_CONFIG). Environment variables with the same name win over this file.
# The file is parsed as KEY=VALUE lines, never executed. Check what is in effect with
# `inodefence doctor`.
#
# Format: one KEY=VALUE per line; `export KEY=VALUE` is accepted; comments on their own line only.
# Refused with an error (instead of silently using another path): a comment after a value
# (`KEY=/path # note`; quote the value or move the comment), and an unmatched quote.
# An empty value (`KEY=`) means "not set": the next source (then the default) applies.
# The repository's own `.env` is never read; only this file location (or INODEFENCE_CONFIG).
#
# Only the two keys below are accepted. Any other key is refused with an error, on purpose:
# - INODEFENCE_RUNTIME_ROOT (disposable experiment directory, default /var/lib/inodefence) is
#   read from the environment only; this file does not change it.
# - Research settings (seed, arm, budget, executed SHA, isolation policy) come from command flags
#   or the frozen preregistration files, never from a user config file.

# Repository root. Needed only when `inodefence` is not an editable install from the clone, or to
# run another clone than the one installed (doctor then says which clone's code target commands
# run). Use an absolute path; a relative one depends on the working directory (doctor: WARN).
# INODEFENCE_HOME=/path/to/InodeFence

# Base folder for default output folders: <base>/inodefence-target-run (verify) and
# <base>/inodefence-explore (explore). Default: your home directory. Must be absolute (`~/...`
# is expanded; a relative path is refused) and outside the repository; keep it out of
# cloud-synced folders (results may hold real violating inputs).
# INODEFENCE_OUTPUT_DIR=/path/to/local/inodefence-outputs
